{% extends "layouts/page.njk" %}

{% set articlesList = collections.post | excludeStubs %}
{% set mainClass = 'content-grid' %}

{% block content %}
  <header>
      <h1 class="special header">
        <span class="strong">David Chico Pham </span>writes on technology, culture, democracy and power.
      </h1>
  </header>
  <section class="paragraph">
      <p>
          I'm a Senior Software Engineer (Privacy) who studied history and sociology, not computer science. I taught myself to code and programming. History trained me to ask why systems are built the way they are and who they serve. Sociology showed me how people actually behave inside those systems. Those turned out to be exactly the right questions for building digital systems. I've been fortunate to work alongside some of the most talented and creative folks in media and technology.
    </p>
    <p>
        As a first-generation Mexican-Vietnamese American, Buddhist from the Midwest, and working-class person, I often felt like an outsider. The concept of "community" seemed abstract and elusive to me. It was something I didn't quite get. I had a hard time grasping its true meaning. However, over time, I've come to understand that "community" is fundamentally about our relationships with one another. This personal site is an entry to the community of indie web creators and thinkers.
    {# <p>In my spare time I work on <a href="/sourdoughs/">making sourdoughs bread</a>, I <a href="/tinker/">tinker</a> with old ipods, and I play a lot <a href='https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198116240122/'>Destiny 2</a> -- Warlock main. You can find me on <a href="/elsewhere/">various online platforms &amp; communities</a>.</p> #}
  </section>

  <section class="paragraph">
    <p>
    <strong><a href="/this-is-my-next/">This is my next</a></strong> is a new section on this site where I share what I'm learning about technology, concepts, and ideas that shape our world and my own thinking. With Agentic AI like Claude Code, what were once side projects collecting dust can now be fully built personal apps. Currently, I'm exploring
    {% set thisIsMyNext = collections.timnPosts %}
    {% if thisIsMyNext and thisIsMyNext.length > 0 %}
      {% set latestTimn = thisIsMyNext | first %}
      <a href="{{ latestTimn.url }}">{{ latestTimn.data.title }}</a>
    {% endif %}
    </p>
    <p>
    I'm simultaneously terrified and elated by Agentic Engineering. Its ability to scaffold and build out apps that fit a person's needs and execute ideas is incredible. I think it's a chance to build a worker-led software revolution.
    </p>
    </section>
  <h4>Chico was my nickname in school.</h4>
  <section id="front-content-display">
     <section>
      <h2 class="text-4xl py-8 pt-4 pb-0">StoryStream</h2>
      <p class="thin pb-4">Findings on the web, interesting stuff, or beautiful things to share</p>
      {% set amplifyItems = collections.contentTypes | findBySlug('amplify') | values('items') %}
      {% set mainFeedItems = raindrop.articles | limit(13) | editorialFeed(amplifyItems) %}
      {% include "components/main-feed.njk" %}

      <p>
        Subscribe to the <a href="/main-feed/feed.xml">Main Feed RSS</a>, the <a href="/amplify/feed.xml">StoryStream RSS</a>, or view the entire <a href="/amplify">archive</a> for more.
      </p>
    </section>
    {% set thoughts = articlesList | onlyTypes(['thought']) %}

    {% if thoughts.length > 0 %}
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-4xl py-8">Recent Thoughts</h2>
        {% set postsList = thoughts | reverse | limit(10) %}
        {% include "components/post-list.njk" %}
        <p>
          View <a href="/thoughts/">more thoughts...</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    {% endif %}

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-4xl pt-4 pb-0 mt-0 content-grid-header">Essays</h2>
      <h3 class="thin pb-4 my-0 content-grid-header">Loose, vague feelings on things I don't entirely understand yet.</h3>
      {% set postsList = articlesList | excludeTypes(['thought', 'project', 'mirror', 'resource', 'amplify']) | reverse | limit(12) %}
      {% include "components/post-list.njk" %}
      <p>
        Subscribe to the <a href="/writing/feed.xml">RSS Feed</a> or view the entire <a href="/writing">archive</a> for more.
      </p>
    </section>

  </section>

  <p>You can find out more <a href="/about/">about me</a>, what I <a href="/uses/">use</a>, the books that I <a href="/books/">have been reading</a> and what I am up to <a href="/now/">now</a>.</p>
{% endblock %}
